WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:02.859
♪I can't keep quiet ♪

00:00:02.859 --> 00:00:06.299
- [Connie] It's really incredible
to watch something become

00:00:06.299 --> 00:00:07.882
bigger than myself.

00:00:08.869 --> 00:00:11.501
I used to call Quiet my song.

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:13.334
Quiet is now our song.

00:00:17.741 --> 00:00:19.280
My name is Connie Lim

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.509
and I go by MILCK as a recording artist

00:00:22.509 --> 00:00:26.009
and I think my job is to help heal people.

00:00:29.068 --> 00:00:31.818
(upbeat strings)

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.181
I got involved with music
by playing piano and singing

00:00:38.181 --> 00:00:41.431
and writing my first song at age seven.

00:00:42.781 --> 00:00:46.948
My mission with my music
is to empower and to heal.

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:51.691
I used to have an eating disorder

00:00:51.691 --> 00:00:54.371
and I am a product of abuse,

00:00:54.371 --> 00:00:58.371
and so when I wrote songs
I was able to digest some

00:00:58.371 --> 00:00:59.288
of my pain.

00:01:00.621 --> 00:01:05.210
I'm constantly chasing the high
of writing a song that makes

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.877
me feel like I can breathe more.

00:01:13.011 --> 00:01:17.178
My song, Quiet, is about
that gentle rage that I felt

00:01:18.731 --> 00:01:21.419
whenever I felt stereotyped,

00:01:21.419 --> 00:01:23.269
or oppressed, or controlled,

00:01:23.269 --> 00:01:27.209
or even when I was doing it to myself.

00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:31.459
I went to D.C. to participate
in the D.C. Women's March

00:01:31.459 --> 00:01:35.381
and I recruited a bunch of
women who lived in the D.C. area

00:01:35.381 --> 00:01:37.381
to sing my song with me.

00:01:38.691 --> 00:01:41.691
♪I can't keep quiet ♪

00:01:43.941 --> 00:01:47.099
When we were singing
on the streets of D.C.,

00:01:47.099 --> 00:01:49.099
we did seven flash mobs.

00:01:49.971 --> 00:01:52.280
And, I thought to myself,
this is my calling,

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.080
my calling is to facilitate
these groups of women to come

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:59.811
together and sing together
because singing can create

00:01:59.811 --> 00:02:00.978
endless bonds.

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:05.549
♪I can't keep quiet ♪

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:12.781
Within two days the video
of us performing had

00:02:12.781 --> 00:02:14.198
14 million views.

00:02:16.629 --> 00:02:18.581
My life is completely changed.

00:02:18.581 --> 00:02:20.760
I've signed with Atlantic Records.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.600
I get messages from women all
over the world saying that

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.141
when they can't get out of
bed, they'll play the song

00:02:26.141 --> 00:02:28.021
so they get out of bed.

00:02:28.021 --> 00:02:29.938
I think that's amazing.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.989
I'm definitely going to
continue down this path

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:41.250
because it's so fulfilling
and so empowering for me

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.000
and for other people.

00:02:44.101 --> 00:02:46.509
I'm empowering women

00:02:46.509 --> 00:02:48.069
and men and all genders in between

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:50.049
and helping people heal,

00:02:50.049 --> 00:02:53.216
and that's exactly what my purpose is.

